<InfoPage title="Editorial Policy" kicker="How we publish" description="Standards for original Lovescape comparisons, primary sources, adult boundaries, and corrections."><h2>Useful before optimized</h2><p>Every page should answer a real reader question. Keywords belong in clear titles, headings, and natural explanations—not repetition or hidden blocks.</p><h2>Primary sources</h2><p>Product claims link to Lovescape's official site and help center where possible. We separate subscription access from Chip spending, avoid presenting marketing as test results, and verify changing models and prices before publication.</p><h2>Adult boundaries</h2><p>Coverage concerns consenting fictional adults. Lovescape says it does not support real-person photo uploads; we do not recommend them. We never request private chats, credentials, or intimate personal images.</p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>Material corrections update the relevant article and its machine-readable modification date. Requests should identify the URL, disputed statement, and a direct source supporting the correction.</p></InfoPage>
